From becb0aaa98c9e802e00afe7d78e3304a416a1aca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:25:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban blocked notification shows the requested
 step, not the worker's status note
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem: the Desktop toast/OS notification for card t_b857cd9d read only "Architecture choice settled;
retain only existing primary portal authentication gate." (the blocked event's payload `reason`), while
the same event carried human_request.action = "Sign in to the Telnyx portal through the agent browser...".
Why 1: completion-notify bodyFor('blocked') returned payload.reason.
Why 2: `reason` is the worker's own free-text status note; the user-facing ask lives in human_request,
  which the notifier never read.
Root (not caught): the test "blocked notifies with the payload reason" enshrined reason-as-body; no test
  fed a technical reason alongside a structured ask.

Fix: blocked with a usable human_request -> title unchanged ("needs your input"), body = action (clipped
to 300 chars), detail = "Why you: <why_human> · <task id>". Blocked without one -> "Task paused" + "The
agent paused this task without naming a step for you. Ask it in chat if you're unsure." (no invented
action, no reason). JSON-text human_request is decoded. New i18n keys in en/ja/zh/zh-hant.
Tests: 4 new + 3 updated (enshrined reason-as-body); 6 RED on the base module, 40/40 GREEN.
